        "original_id": "75f745f3-3f36-528d-b8f2-bb1a33862d89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Mosuo Sisters, The Silent Historian\n- People: Marlo Poras, Simonka de Jong\n- Places: China, Beijing, Himalayas, New York\n- Organizations: New York Jewish Film Festival, Jewish Museum, Film Society of Lincoln Center\n- Topics: Mosuo culture, ethnic minorities, documentary films\n\nFacts:\n- The Silent Historian is a 2011 Dutch documentary film by Simonka de Jong.\n- The Mosuo Sisters is a 2012 documentary film written and directed by Marlo Poras.\n- The Silent Historian was shown as part of the January 2012 New York Jewish Film Festival in partnership with the Jewish Museum and Film Society of Lincoln Center.\n- The Mosuo Sisters follows ethnic minority sisters in China as they move from bar work in Beijing back to their village in the Himalayas.\n- The Mosuo Sisters explores how the modern world affects traditional Mosuo culture and way of life.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
